## Why This Question Is Asked
This question tests dynamic programming intuition on a constrained path counting problem with simple transitions and boundary conditions.

## Key Concepts
- **Recurrence relation:** f(i) = f(i+1) + f(i+2) with modulo arithmetic
- **Memoization vs. tabulation:** Trade-offs between recursive top-down with caching versus iterative bottom-up approaches
- **Edge conditions:** Blocked start/end positions, single-cell arrays

## Code Example
```javascript
function countPaths(blocked) {
  const n = blocked.length;
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  if (blocked[0]) return 0;

  // Memoized DFS
  const memo = Array(n).fill(-1);
  function dfs(i) {
    if (i === n - 1) return blocked[i] ? 0 : 1;
    if (i >= n || blocked[i]) return 0;
    if (memo[i] !== -1) return memo[i];
    memo[i] = (dfs(i + 1) + dfs(i + 2)) % MOD;
    return memo[i];
  }
  return dfs(0);
}

// Bottom-up DP (O(1) space)
function countPathsDP(blocked) {
  const n = blocked.length;
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  if (blocked[0]) return 0;

  let next2 = 1, next1 = blocked[n - 1] ? 0 : 1;
  for (let i = n - 2; i >= 0; i--) {
    const curr = blocked[i] ? 0 : (next1 + next2) % MOD;
    next2 = next1;
    next1 = curr;
  }
  return next1;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Intersects BFS path counting and graph pruning under constraints; tests meticulous edge-case handling.

## Key Concepts
- BFS for unweighted shortest paths
- Path counting with modulo arithmetic
- Handling blocked nodes and unreachable cases
- Complexity: O(N+M)

## Code Example
```javascript
function shortestPaths(n, edges, blocked, s, t) {
  const g = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
  for (const [v, u] of edges) if (!blocked[v] && !blocked[u]) g[v].push(u);
  const dist = Array(n).fill(Infinity);
  const ways = Array(n).fill(0);
  if (blocked[s] || blocked[t]) return { dist: -1, ways: 0 };
  dist[s] = 0; ways[s] = 1;
  const q = [s];
  while (q.length) {
    const v = q.shift();
    for (const u of g[v]) {
      if (dist[u] === Infinity) {
        dist[u] = dist[v] + 1; ways[u] = ways[v]; q.push(u);
      } else if (dist[u] === dist[v] + 1) {
        ways[u] = (ways[u] + ways[v]) % 1000000007;
      }
    }
  }
  return { dist: dist[t] === Infinity ? -1 : dist[t], ways: ways[t] };
}
```

